# Ground for one TileMapLayer: grass, dirt and tilled soil, and every transition
# between grass and dirt. Light from the top left; grass stands slightly above dirt.
#
# Tilled soil is darker plain soil with broken furrows and a few lit ridge dashes.
#
# The transition tiles were computed from one grass mask per tile (four wobbly
# boundary profiles, all 4 px deep where they meet the tile's sides), with one light
# rule: grass facing dirt below or right is the shaded bank G, grass facing dirt
# above or left the lit lip L, and dirt just below or right of grass gets the cast
# shadow D. Outer corners are two edges' masks combined, inner corners their overlap,
# so every piece meets the next at the same depth.
#
# Atlas order (columns 4) reads like a dirt patch: corners and edges around dirt,
# inner corners on the right, then the base tiles and the second edge versions.
tileset ground
palette farm
columns 4

part grass_tex
  gggggggGLGgggggg
  gLgLggggggggGggg
  gGLGgggggggggggg
  ggggglgggLgLgggg
  gggggggggGLGgggg
  LgggggGgggggggLg
  GgggggggggggggGL
  ggggggggggggglgg
  ggggLgLggggggggg
  ggggGLGggggggggg
  lggggggggggLgLgg
  gggggggggggGLGgg
  gggggggggGgggggg
  ggLgLggggggggggg
  ggGLGgggggggggGg
  gggggggLgLgggggg
end
part dirt_tex
  dddddddddddddddd
  ddTdddddddDddddd
  dddddddddddddddd
  dddddDdddddddTdd
  dddddddddddddddd
